{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520139-balance-wyrm","id":1520139,"title":"Balance Wyrm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-08T11:25:35-07:00","id":1520139,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Balance Wyrm","content":"What do you think would happen if the Wyrm became balanced again? Mainly wondering what the Black Spiral Dancers and Fomori would do. I think the Wyrm balancing out would cause a schism in the Dancers, some of them doing the same things they used to without any spiritual backing and the rest serving the new Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28099-cardassianartistry","name":"CardassianArtistry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28099_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T12:14:22-07:00","id":1520141,"title":"","content":"In what has been a multiple campaign series of games my SO and I have run/played, we had to answer this question as our current setting is in a post Apocalypse, the Wyrm/Triat was brought back into balance, world. At least for some of it as we're doing our own take on the story ideas presented in Shattered Dreams.<br /> <br /> In our take of the post Apocalypse world, the Spirals are split into three factions. There are those who still want to be like the tribe was and act as such. They refuse to believe the Wyrm returning to balance is a good thing. There are those who are all on board with serving the Wyrm in its new balanced state. These Spirals have all revised the Spiral after the Wyrm was returned to balance and came back with new revelations on their purpose. If the opportunity presents itself, they will capture members of the formerly mentioned group and force them into the Spiral so they too can gain those revelations. And lastly there are those currently obsessed with the idea of trying to become the White Howlers again and thus trying to regain Lion's favor.<br /> <br /> As for the Formori and other Wyrm beings, they are also split between refusing to change or falling in line with the Wyrm's new goals.<br /> <br /> Overall, those who fall in line generally aid in hunting down those who have not, as those who have not are seen as the remnant's of the Wyrm's past sickness that needs to be purged so the Wyrm can finish its healing process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27780-scaperdeage","name":"ScaperDeage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27780_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T12:21:27-07:00","id":1520142,"title":"","content":"Tremendous upheaval in the cosmos that wrecks a lot of shit, followed by a non-twisted and healthy universe. This is demonstrated in Apocalypse after completion of the rite to free and heal the Wyrm. As the universe is still unbalanced upon its return, well, it does destroy an awful lot, but the resulting growth back is healthy, for once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T12:52:09-07:00","id":1520146,"title":"","content":"In my chronicles the Balance Wyrm and the Wyrm are two distinct entities. The Balance Wyrm is just the embodiment of decay and death in the natural world. The Wyrm is the cause of supernatural evil - and what exactly it is, isn't clear. The Wyrm as Garou know it is one possibility. So is Satan or Nidhogg or Tiamat or Ahriman or Apep or the Prince of Darkness or Nyarlathtoep. The myth about the Balance Wyrm becoming the Wyrm is just Garou legendry to explain the philosophical Problem of Evil. It is not any more right (or wrong) than other reasons people give for the Problem of Evil in their own religion. The Garou know a lot of things about the spirit world, but they don't know everything.<br /> <br /> Eschatology demands that any solution to the Problem of Evil (and hence things like restoring the Balance Wyrm if that is applicable in your chronicles) is done through the Apocalypse. It is the end of the old world, with all its problems and evils, that allows for a purified new world that will not have those problems. That is just how apocalypses work. If the foundation of supernatural evil ends, so does evil. So in a scenario where the Balance Wyrm is the Wyrm, and the Wyrm returns to Balance, than the BSDs and fomori and vampires and everything else also ends. We don't get our world (even a WoD version of it) and the game continues. We have a purified new world without the taint of evil (or for those who are more nihilistic, evil triumphant). <br /> <br /> A true post-apocalyptic world is not one that is actually playable because there won't be anything to do. If you are playing in a &quot;Post-apocalyptic&quot; world, I think it is one best understood as one where the Apocalypse has clearly begun... but it's not over yet. Way worse things will still come before the final battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T19:40:28-07:00","id":1520167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520139-balance-wyrm?p=1520146#post1520146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my chronicles the Balance Wyrm and the Wyrm are two distinct entities. The Balance Wyrm is just the embodiment of decay and death in the natural world. The Wyrm is the cause of supernatural evil - and what exactly it is, isn't clear. The Wyrm as Garou know it is one possibility. So is Satan or Nidhogg or Tiamat or Ahriman or Apep or the Prince of Darkness or Nyarlathtoep. The myth about the Balance Wyrm becoming the Wyrm is just Garou legendry to explain the philosophical Problem of Evil. It is not any more right (or wrong) than other reasons people give for the Problem of Evil in their own religion. The Garou know a lot of things about the spirit world, but they don't know everything.<br /> <br /> Eschatology demands that any solution to the Problem of Evil (and hence things like restoring the Balance Wyrm if that is applicable in your chronicles) is done through the Apocalypse. It is the end of the old world, with all its problems and evils, that allows for a purified new world that will not have those problems. That is just how apocalypses work. If the foundation of supernatural evil ends, so does evil. So in a scenario where the Balance Wyrm is the Wyrm, and the Wyrm returns to Balance, than the BSDs and fomori and vampires and everything else also ends. We don't get our world (even a WoD version of it) and the game continues. We have a purified new world without the taint of evil (or for those who are more nihilistic, evil triumphant).<br /> <br /> A true post-apocalyptic world is not one that is actually playable because there won't be anything to do. If you are playing in a &quot;Post-apocalyptic&quot; world, I think it is one best understood as one where the Apocalypse has clearly begun... but it's not over yet. Way worse things will still come before the final battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting take on it. I've always conceptualized it as the God from Demon and Vampire having created reality, and the Triat being a natural product of life's existence. That is to say anywhere life exists chaos, order, and decay exist as well. The various spirits also naturally sprang into existence as soon as their material counterparts did. An odd piece of headcanon I have is that Gaea is not the manifestation of Earth but of life. This is sort of supported by the fact that Luna and Helios are Celestines, but Gaea is said to be above that level.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ScaperDeage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520139-balance-wyrm?p=1520141#post1520141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what has been a multiple campaign series of games my SO and I have run/played, we had to answer this question as our current setting is in a post Apocalypse, the Wyrm/Triat was brought back into balance, world. At least for some of it as we're doing our own take on the story ideas presented in Shattered Dreams.<br /> <br /> In our take of the post Apocalypse world, the Spirals are split into three factions. There are those who still want to be like the tribe was and act as such. They refuse to believe the Wyrm returning to balance is a good thing. There are those who are all on board with serving the Wyrm in its new balanced state. These Spirals have all revised the Spiral after the Wyrm was returned to balance and came back with new revelations on their purpose. If the opportunity presents itself, they will capture members of the formerly mentioned group and force them into the Spiral so they too can gain those revelations. And lastly there are those currently obsessed with the idea of trying to become the White Howlers again and thus trying to regain Lion's favor.<br /> <br /> As for the Formori and other Wyrm beings, they are also split between refusing to change or falling in line with the Wyrm's new goals.<br /> <br /> Overall, those who fall in line generally aid in hunting down those who have not, as those who have not are seen as the remnant's of the Wyrm's past sickness that needs to be purged so the Wyrm can finish its healing process.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty cool, I somehow never considered that some of them might want to rejoin the Nation. However, I think a lot of Garou wouldn't want them back. I did imagine that Pentex and old Wyrm remnants might capture wyrmish spirits and redeemed BSDs and try to torture them into becoming as they were before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28099-cardassianartistry","name":"CardassianArtistry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28099_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T22:04:49-07:00","id":1520171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's pretty cool, I somehow never considered that some of them might want to rejoin the Nation. However, I think a lot of Garou wouldn't want them back. I did imagine that Pentex and old Wyrm remnants might capture wyrmish spirits and redeemed BSDs and try to torture them into becoming as they were before. </div> </div> </div>A lot of this outcome just has to do with the plots of and how events played out in our Apocalypse game, which was a 5 year long campaign, so would be a lot to go into. A very basic rundown is our World of Darkness existed as one of the keystone worlds within the Dark Tower universe, if you are familiar with it, so there was a threat beyond the whole Triat is out of whack issue. Plus we went with all of the Triat was a danger to everyone's existence and were in all out war with each other. The Wyrm even ended up the weakest faction because of how events played out.<br /> <br /> Anyway, during that game we did manage to mostly bring major groups of shifters together, which then expanded past that to vampires, mages, and so on. The Apocalypse in our game occured over 10 years and survivors split into two main groups, one siding with Queen Ananasa's plans and the other remained more neutral. Once it was all over and the Wyrm was healed/freed and the cycle of destruction and resetting stopped, those two large survivor groups reconnected and been trying to rebuild both society and a heavily damaged planet. There is a Council that acts as a ruling body made up of representatives for pretty much everything you could name. In the present day time, the Spirals are a new addition to the Council and sure, there are those not happy about it, but the Council voted to give them a chance and as long as they follow the rules. Besides, after the Wyrm itself was healed, it's really hard to make the argument that Spirals have no right to a second chance, never mind that the Council already consisted of lots of strange bedfellows anyway. <br /> <br /> Our current game's general plot is pretty much all about the remnants of the old Wyrm trying to alter time to prevent the resolution to how the Apocalypse resolved. We're all legendary individuals that were part of significant events throughout time and tossed together as a pack to stop it. I've been playing my character from the Apocalypse game since she was pretty much the main reason the Wyrm ended up healed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27780-scaperdeage","name":"ScaperDeage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27780_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T03:52:45-07:00","id":1520180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520139-balance-wyrm?p=1520146#post1520146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyrm as Garou know it is one possibility. So is Satan or Nidhogg or Tiamat or Ahriman or Apep or the Prince of Darkness or Nyarlathtoep. The myth about the Balance Wyrm becoming the Wyrm is just Garou legendry to explain the philosophical Problem of Evil. It is not any more right (or wrong) than other reasons people give for the Problem of Evil in their own religion. The Garou know a lot of things about the spirit world, but they don't know everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the balance wyrm becoming the fallen wyrm is no garou mythology. It is confirmed by many entities which observed the fall, such as the dragon of forgetfullness in the garou tribes novel, or Ananasa. And confirmed OOC many times, including in the very cosmology chapter of the original book of Wyrm, which is written out of character.<br /> <br /> Nor is the fall of the Wyrm the start of Evil in most garou's mythologies. Sure, it might be when shit hit the fan, but evil preexisted it. After all. The garoua attribute the fall to an act of evil from the Weaver pre corrupt Wyrm, and many garou legends have terrible events and evil entities coming from before the fall, such as the legend of the bloody man.<br /> <br /> In fact, the very existence of the balance Wyrm imply that the world was never perfect, if it was,would be not need for a balance keeper.<br /> <br /> Balance Wyrm which was never a perfect balance keeper, since(based on the classical cosmological history) it allowed the Weaver to separate the worlds of flesh and spirit, which is described, OOC, as one one of most unbalanlanced act ever and the unmistakable sign of the Weaver's growing madness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520139-balance-wyrm?p=1520146#post1520146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eschatology demands that any solution to the Problem of Evil (and hence things like restoring the Balance Wyrm if that is applicable in your chronicles) is done through the Apocalypse. It is the end of the old world, with all its problems and evils, that allows for a purified new world that will not have those problems. That is just how apocalypses work. If the foundation of supernatural evil ends, so does evil. So in a scenario where the Balance Wyrm is the Wyrm, and the Wyrm returns to Balance, than the BSDs and fomori and vampires and everything else also ends. We don't get our world (even a WoD version of it) and the game continues. We have a purified new world without the taint of evil (or for those who are more nihilistic, evil triumphant).</div> </div> </div> </div>this scenario doesn't necessarily end evil though, since it would bring the world back to the original point, where evil already happened thanks to the Weaver. In the best ending of the Weaver ascendant scenario, the Weaver recognise her mistakes. But we don't know if she'll stay that way, or if the question of ultimate purpose won't lighten her madness up again.<br /> <br /> Nor is it garanteed that the return of the balance Wyrm will necessarily snap the Weaver from her maniacal ways. We may end up with an out out war between a rejuvenated balance Wyrm and an overpowered Weaver.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520139-balance-wyrm?p=1520146#post1520146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> A true post-apocalyptic world is not one that is actually playable because there won't be anything to do. If you are playing in a &quot;Post-apocalyptic&quot; world, I think it is one best understood as one where the Apocalypse has clearly begun... but it's not over yet. Way worse things will still come before the final battle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's still things to be done in a world of darkness where the Wyrm is healed. In fact, one of the possible way to do so was from an alternative setting created in on of the storyteller's guides if I remember correcly, where the clash between Wyld and Weaver is the cause of all harm, and the garous are under tje patronage of the balance Wyrm to save Gaia from thr clash between Order and Chaos.<br /> <br /> In the scenario of his return, we might also wonder what will happens to humanity, after all, they're unbalanced as hell, completly belonging to the Weaver with a few exception.<br /> <br /> same for vampires and other such entities. Sure the balance wyrm will target them, but could he kill them? We don't know how powerful he would be post healing. As far as we know, he could be as much reduced to acting through agents on Earth as the other two.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T06:06:27-07:00","id":1520190,"title":"","content":"It's important to remember that both the Wyrm and Weaver are crazy. Even if the Wyrm gets &quot;fixed&quot; the Weaver is still mad and out of control. If anything, fixing the Wyrm would likely drive the Weaver to an even greater state of insanity. It went crazy and trapped and twisted the Wyrm in the first place because the Wyrm was only destroying everything. If Wyrm returned to its destroyer aspect, that would likely result in the Weaver breaking even worse than it is now. <br /> <br /> You'd probably see some Wyrm minions, mainly spirits, convert their loyalty to the &quot;new&quot; Wyrm. But you'd likely see many minions, Black Spirals who are insane, various spirits that are more about corruption than destruction, Pentex and various high ranking Wyrm minions who would stand to lose their position in the new hierarchy breaking off. I suspect that a number of them would end up joining an insane Weaver. If I were to use this in a campaign, I would have a thoroughly broken Weaver begin absorbing those corruptive aspects that the healed Wyrm sheds into itself. That would then set the stage for a story that involves permanently putting down the Weaver (and possibly replacing it with Ananasa as was suggested as a possible outcome in the older books). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520139-balance-wyrm?p=1520180#post1520180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, the very existence of the balance Wyrm imply that the world was never perfect, if it was,would be not need for a balance keeper.\u200b<br /> <br /> Balance Wyrm which was never a perfect balance keeper, since(based on the classical cosmological history) it allowed the Weaver to separate the worlds of flesh and spirit, which is described, OOC, as one one of most unbalanlanced act ever and the unmistakable sign of the Weaver's growing madness.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Balance Wyrm&quot; is a bit of misnomer. The original Wyrm was the Destroyer Wyrm and it was the force of entropy that destroyed everything. It never really had anything to do with balancing. Rather, the phrase &quot;Balance Wyrm&quot; refers to the way the Triat used to be balanced before the Wyrm became the Corruptor Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T08:22:24-07:00","id":1520200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520139-balance-wyrm?p=1520190#post1520190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Balance Wyrm&quot; is a bit of misnomer. The original Wyrm was the Destroyer Wyrm and it was the force of entropy that destroyed everything. It never really had anything to do with balancing. Rather, the phrase &quot;Balance Wyrm&quot; refers to the way the Triat used to be balanced before the Wyrm became the Corruptor Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely. This aspect was developped in the OOC part of the original 2 books of the Wyrm, with the balance Wyrm not merely destroying, but also influencing regrowth. It's role is described as both destroying the influence of the other two mepber of the triats when they were walking on the other's turf, but also helping the weaker one.<br /> <br /> Once trapped, the Wyrm is described as no longuer be able to do either, so found a third way, which is described as &quot;not destruction, nor regrowth, but something in between, transformation. Twisting itself and the world to serve it's purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}